file: "packages/ops/src/render/render_op_error.ts"
doc: "RenderOpError: boundary Error class thrown from renderOp.execute when any pipeline stage fails."

structs: [
  { name: "RenderOpError"
    doc:
      "Boundary error thrown out of renderOp.execute. Flattens the four "
      "typed-Result stage errors (LoadError, ResolveError, LayoutError, "
      "RenderError) into a single throwable.\n"
      "\n"
      "MUST extend `Error` — main.ts's catch block calls `err.message` (per "
      "ops_framework/cli_main.spec.textproto step 8). A plain object would "
      "stringify as \"[object Object]\" via the `String(err)` fallback, which "
      "produces a useless error message.\n"
      "\n"
      "Emit exactly (override the contract-skeleton's `class { stage!: string; "
      "cause!: unknown; }` rendering — the agent's job is to emit the class "
      "form below, not a plain data class):\n"
      "\n"
      "  // SPDX-License-Identifier: AGPL-3.0-or-later\n"
      "\n"
      "  import type { LoadError } from '@archeglyph/core/loaders';\n"
      "  import type { ResolveError } from '@archeglyph/core/resolver/resolve_error';\n"
      "  import type { LayoutError } from '@archeglyph/core/layout/layout_error';\n"
      "  import type { RenderError } from '@archeglyph/core/renderer/render_error';\n"
      "\n"
      "  export type RenderStage = 'load' | 'resolve' | 'layout' | 'render';\n"
      "\n"
      "  export type RenderStageError = LoadError | ResolveError | LayoutError | RenderError;\n"
      "\n"
      "  export class RenderOpError extends Error {\n"
      "    readonly stage: RenderStage;\n"
      "    readonly cause: RenderStageError;\n"
      "    constructor(stage: RenderStage, cause: RenderStageError) {\n"
      "      super(`render: ${stage}: ${cause.message}`);\n"
      "      this.name = 'RenderOpError';\n"
      "      this.stage = stage;\n"
      "      this.cause = cause;\n"
      "    }\n"
      "  }\n"
      "\n"
      "Why a class extending Error rather than a discriminated-union literal:\n"
      "  1. `throw err` produces `err.message` in main.ts's catch via "
      "Error.message; a plain object loses this.\n"
      "  2. `instanceof RenderOpError` lets callers (future tests, MCP wrapper) "
      "do structural narrowing without sniffing the .stage field.\n"
      "  3. The `stage`/`cause` fields carry the discriminated-union value "
      "cleanly for callers that want to inspect classification.\n"
      "\n"
      "Note: spec declares `cause` as type `unsupported` because TS unions "
      "at type position don't lift through the textproto schema (Koine "
      "cascading-loss pattern). The emit-shape above resolves this with the "
      "explicit `RenderStageError` type alias."
    fields: [
      { name: "stage", type: { primitive: CHARACTER } },
      { name: "cause", type: { unsupported: { reason: UNION_AT_TYPE_POSITION } } }
    ]
    typescript: {}
  }
]
